<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on Aug 6.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on Aug 6.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed</p>
<p>Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Fortune Navigator   SLD Jly 28	 5,000	 Vietnam</p>
<p>Burgos		  SLD Aug 02	14,000	 Vladivostok</p>
<p>Navigator D	   SLD Jly 31	12,500	 Japan</p>
<p>Gang Nam		SLD Jly 31	 5,000	 India</p>
<p>Billion		 SLD Aug 03	 6,100	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Dibena Express	SLD Jly 31	 7,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Bong Hoa San	  SLD Jly 29	   400	 N.Korea</p>
<p>Jutha Suphannika    ETD Aug 06	12,000	 Japan</p>
<p>Alam Tankas	   ETD Aug 09	15,000	 Malaysia</p>
<p>RCL-A		   ETB Aug 04	 1,100	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Tasmia		  N/A		 12,000	 Mombaza</p>
<p>Yuan Jiang	    N/A		 14,000	 Pakistan</p>
<p>Jutha Rachavadee    ETA Aug 04	12,000	 Japan</p>
<p>Am Nok Gang	   Cancelled</p>
<p>Bangbua		 Cancelled</p>
<p>Orient Express I    ETA Aug 14	 1,200	 Cambodia</p>
<p>Bangramad	     ETA Aug 06	 5,800	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Delight		 ETA Aug 18	 5,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Sun Folcon	    ETA Aug 21	18,000	 Japan</p>
<p>Jia He Guan	   ETA Aug 07	 5,700	 Japan</p>
<p>Accord		  ETA Aug 07	 7,000	 Vietnam</p>
<p>Aro		     ETA Aug 13	18,000	 Japan</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
